00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:34.713
But we want to dry-run it first.

00:11:34.713 --> 00:11:37.130
So we want to be able to have
a look at exactly where this

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:37.830
is going to go.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:40.038
So we have a lot of feelings
of confidence and safety

00:11:40.038 --> 00:11:41.460
in what it is that we're doing.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.250
So, here we can see
we have a config v1,

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.170
and we can see that
it's being applied

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:47.995
to each of the clusters that
are around the globe, all four

00:11:47.995 --> 00:11:49.620
of them, which is
exactly what we want.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:50.790
So we're like, great,
that's awesome.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.320
That's exactly what we want.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.250
So now let's run that
again with no dry run.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:59.670
And we'll see that's now
going to start pushing it out

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.225
