00:13:34.588 --> 00:13:35.880
It's going to do an allocation.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.980
For those of you who aren't
familiar with Agones,

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:41.010
an allocation is basically
a special thing that says,

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.140
OK, give me a game
server and then mark it

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:46.110
as allocated so that I know
that there are players playing

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.690
on that particular game server.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:47.880
Right?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:48.600
And don't delete it.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:49.710
We don't want to
delete game servers

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.060
where players are playing.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.100
They tend to get mad
when that happens.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.770
So we got back a game
server, which is awesome.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.280
Let's actually kubectl
